<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT - Nadro raised to buy.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Nadro raised to buy.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican brokerage Accival said on Monday it raised its recommendation on pharmaceutical company Nadro to buy from neutral.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect good second quarter results will continue to push Nadro's stock price,&quot; analyst Cecilia del Castillo wrote in a report.  </p>
<p>Del Castillo set a year-end price estimate for Nadro of 33 pesos and estimated sales for 1997 will grow 9.5 percent compared to the previous year.</p>
<p>The company's shares stood at 24.50 pesos in late trading on Monday, down 30 centavos from Friday's close.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
